From 1298e17ed16cf8b56a6c1bfde6dc9841e60eedec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mkinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 15:16:03 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(machines): Tormach lathes state spindle.rigid_tapping
 from the manuals

The 8L, 15L Slant-PRO and 15LX Slant-PRO files now state
"rigid_tapping": true. Each operator manual (UM10753 10.3.18, UM10225
6.5.17, UM10860 10.3.13) has a G33.1 rigid-tapping section. The pin
every_tormach_mill_router_and_lathe_file_states_rigid_tapping now
checks the three lathes. Posted output does not change: the gate
refuses only a stated false, and tormach-lathe.cps still refuses TAP.

Fixes #795

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
